%I A402500 #18 Nov 22 2026 12:33:19
%S A402500 17,41,281,6161,80081,680681,12932921,594914321,8626257641,
%T A402500 267413986841,9894317513081,811334036072561,34887363551120081,
%U A402500 819853043451321881,86904422605840119281,2563680466872283518761,156384508479209294644361,10477762068107022741172121,1487842213671197229246441041
%N A402500 a(n) is the number equal to either (4/3)*prime(n)# + 1 or (8/3)*prime(n)# + 1 that is not divisible by 3, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402500 For n >= 2, a(n) == 1 (mod 8) is a quadratic residue modulo every prime 5 <= p <= prime(n).
%C A402500 By requiring a(n) not being divisible by 3, sequence forms a compatible system modulo {A102476(n+1)=4*prime(n)#}: a(n) mod 4*prime(m)# = a(m) for n >= m >= 2.
%C A402500 Let N = A102476(n+1) be the least modulus with 2^(n+1) square roots of 1. The minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing a(n), or the least m coprime to N such that a(n)/m is a square modulo N, is m = A401356(n-1). Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402500 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if 3 divides D.
%H A402500 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402500/b402500.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..350</a>
%F A402500 Let b(n) = A340764(prime(n)) be the number of primes p <= prime(n) that are congruent to 2 modulo 3. Then a(n) = (4/3)*prime(n)# + 1 if b(n) is even and (8/3)*prime(n)# + 1 if b(n) is odd.
%F A402500 a(n) = A102476(n+1) - A402505(n).
%o A402500 (PARI) my(P=8, pi32=1); forprime(p=5, 100, print1(if(pi32==0, P+1, 2*P+1), ", "); P*=p; if(p%3==2, pi32=1-pi32))
%Y A402500 Cf. A002110, A102476, A340764, A402431, A401356.
%Y A402500 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402500 nonn,easy,new
%O A402500 2,1
